From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:24:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: bound the ycbcr conversion lookup in every build

lookup_ycbcr_conversion() asserted that the set, and the binding in it,
exist in the pipeline layouts, and read the binding's immutable samplers
through them. The asserts compile out of a release build, which then
read past the layout's bindings for a binding it does not hold and used
what it found as a sampler pointer.

Return no conversion for a set or binding the layouts do not hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index cf85c52ee535220910bd324947911a2eca139aab..c8399f59c1d7874ff0a14c39b3f323efd9c05a49 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -253,11 +253,17 @@ lookup_ycbcr_conversion(const void *_state, uint32_t set, uint32_t binding,
                         uint32_t array_index)
 {
    const struct lower_ycbcr_state *state = _state;
-   assert(set < state->set_layout_count);
-   assert(state->set_layouts[set] != NULL);
+
+   /* A binding the layouts do not hold has no conversion. The bounds are
+    * checked in every build: an assert compiles out of a release build, which
+    * then reads the immutable samplers of a binding past the layout's. */
+   if (set >= state->set_layout_count || state->set_layouts[set] == NULL)
+      return NULL;
+
    const struct kk_descriptor_set_layout *set_layout =
       vk_to_kk_descriptor_set_layout(state->set_layouts[set]);
-   assert(binding < set_layout->binding_count);
+   if (binding >= set_layout->binding_count)
+      return NULL;
 
    const struct kk_descriptor_set_binding_layout *bind_layout =
       &set_layout->binding[binding];
